BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: NJ Bowling, Volleyball, Tennis & More
UID:event_316259946@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260905T041736Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260905T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260905T220000
SUMMARY:NJ Singles Day Trip to NYC: Soulmate Photobooth\, Dancing & Villag
 e Stroll
DESCRIPTION:North Jersey Bowling\, Volleyball\, Tennis & More\n**One train
  ride. A whole day in the city. And you don't have to bring anyone.**\nThi
 s is a **singles day trip from New Jersey into New York City** on the Satu
 rday of Labor Day weekend. We meet at Newark Penn Station\, ride in togeth
 er\, and spend the day doing three genuinely fun things with a group of pe
 ople who all showed up for the same reason: to meet someone in real life i
 nstead of on an app.\nNo icebreaker circles. No name tags. No one making y
 ou introduce yourself to the room. Just a good day out where meeting peopl
 e happens naturally.\n\\*\\*\\*\n**☕ 10:00 AM — Meet at Newark Penn St
 ation** Main concourse\, by the NJ Transit departure board. I'll be postin
 g what I will be wearing on the day before — look for me. Come at 9:50 i
 f you're nervous\; I'll be there early and we'll talk before anyone else s
 hows up. *We leave at 10:20 sharp. Please be on time — we can't hold the
  group.*\n**🚆 10:20 AM — Into the city together** **\\- Transit to Ne
 w York Penn Station\\\, about 20 minutes\\\,** Buy your ticket before you 
 get there so we're not all in line at once. We ride together\, which means
  the awkward part is over before we even arrive.\n**📸 11:00 AM — The 
 Soulmate Photobooth** **The Missed Connections Booth — outside Santo Tac
 o\, 94 University Place at E 12th St\, Union Square\, Manhattan.** You sca
 n a QR code\, answer a short compatibility quiz\, and step into the booth.
  It prints two strips: one of you\, and one of the stranger the algorithm 
 picked as your match. **$10.** It's the best icebreaker in New York. By th
 e time we walk away\, everyone's comparing strips and laughing\, and nobod
 y's a stranger anymore.\n**🌮 12:30 PM — Lunch around Union Square** S
 anto Taco is right there\, and there's everything else within two blocks 
 — sit-down\, quick\, veggie\, whatever you're in the mood for. **We can 
 stop by whenever. This is just tentative.**\n**🚶🏽‍♀️ 2:00 PM 
 — Stroll through Greenwich Village** Down through **Washington Square Pa
 rk**\, then into the **West Village** — the brownstones\, the little str
 eets\, the sidewalk musicians. Easy pace\, lots of stopping\, lots of talk
 ing. This is the part where the real conversations happen. About 2 miles t
 otal\, all flat\, and we stop whenever people want to.\n**💃🏽 5:00 PM
  — Dancing**\\- TBA\\. **No partner needed. No experience needed.** If y
 ou haven't danced in fifteen years\, you're in good company — half of us
  haven't either. Come for one song and stay for six.\n**🌙 8:00 PM — H
 ead home\, or stay out** We'll walk back toward the train together around 
 8. Stay later if the night's going well — you're a grown adult\, nobody'
 s checking.\n\\*\\*\\*\n**Who this is for** Single adults **21 and over** 
 who want to meet people face to face. Our crowd is a real mix\, and it usu
 ally lands around 25+.The vibe is grown\, warm\, and easygoing — good co
 nversation and good music\, not a college bar night.\n**Come alone.** Almo
 st everyone does. That's the entire point.\n**What it costs** Free to RSVP
 . You cover your own day:\nNo hidden fees\, nothing collected up front\, n
 o upsell.\n**Good to know**\n\n* We're walking about 2–3 miles across th
 e day\, all flat. Wear shoes you'd walk a city in.\n* **Bring Cash**\n* Th
 ere's alcohol at the dance venue\, and **absolutely no pressure to drink**
 . Plenty of us won't be.\n* Rain or shine. If the weather turns\, the stro
 ll becomes a longer lunch and we go dance early.\n* Bring a portable charg
 er. You'll take more photos than you think.\n\n**Important Policies**\n**W
 eather & Rain Date Policy:** This event may be postponed or rescheduled du
 e to rain\, severe weather\, unsafe conditions\, or circumstances beyond t
 he organizers’ control. If the event is postponed\, all tickets will aut
 omatically transfer to the announced rain date or rescheduled date. Refund
 s will not be issued if a ticket holder is unable to attend the new date. 
 If the event is canceled by the organizers and no replacement date is sche
 duled\, attendees will be contacted regarding available options.\n**Liabil
 ity and Assumption of Risk:** Participation is voluntary. Neither Yes We T
 hryve\, NJ Singles\, Catholic Singles NJ\, nor their organizers\, voluntee
 rs\, instructors\, venues\, or hosts shall be responsible for any injury\,
  illness\, loss\, theft\, or property damage occurring during or in connec
 tion with the event\, to the fullest extent permitted by law.\n**Photograp
 hy and Consent:** Photos and videos may be taken during the event for mark
 eting\, promotional\, and community purposes. By attending\, you consent t
 o the use of your image in future promotions. Please notify an organizer a
 t the event if you prefer not to be photographed or recorded.\n**Email Sub
 scription:** By RSVPing\, you agree to be added to the Yes We Thryve and N
 J Singles email lists for event announcements and community updates. You m
 ay unsubscribe at any time.\n**Respect and Courtesy:** Please be kind and 
 respectful toward venue staff\, organizers\, volunteers\, and fellow guest
 s. Disruptive\, threatening\, discriminatory\, or inappropriate behavior m
 ay result in removal from the event without a refund.\n**Arrival and Depar
 ture:** You are welcome to arrive late or leave early unless the event des
 cription states otherwise. This is intended to be a friendly\, inclusive\,
  and low-pressure environment where guests can connect in person.\n**Ticke
 t Policy:** All sales are final. Tickets are nonrefundable and non-transfe
 rable\, except where otherwise stated by the organizers.
